# File: tests/features/add_greeting_words_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/319-add-greeting-words-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Return the whitespace-separated words of the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Return the greeting's words for single-word names
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_words is called with Ada and Zo plus U+00EB
    Then the results are Hello, Ada and Hello, Zo plus U+00EB as word lists
    And each result equals the split of the greeting

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Split multi-word names on any whitespace run
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_words is called with Ada Lovelace and Ada space-tab-space Lovelace
    Then both results are the words Hello, Ada, and Lovelace
    And each result length equals greeting_word_count of the same name

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_words is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing the CLI
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_words of Ada
    Then it prints the list Hello, and Ada and greeting_words is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the word list of the complete greeting and the inherited invalid-name error
    And nmg-smoke Ada still prints exactly Hello, Ada and exits with status 0

